course: dictionary
lesson: 5007
title: Infected: germs and clues
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Infected means having harmful germs growing in something. Germs are tiny living things that can make you ill. The context often gives you clues: «A splinter left in can get infected.» The word left in and the idea of germs getting into skin tell you what infected means here.
explain: Look for signs in the sentence. «The cut was red, swollen and sore.» Red, swollen and sore are signs that germs are growing in the cut, so the cut is infected. Doctors and nurses use these clues to spot infections.
explain: The same word works for computers and feelings. «The computer was infected with a virus, so it lost its files.» Here it means a harmful program is inside. «The whole class was infected by her laughter.» Here it means a feeling spread from one person to everyone.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. «A splinter left in can get germs growing in it» still makes sense, so infected means the same thing. Each time, ask: does my meaning fit the sentence?
fact: Infected means having harmful germs growing in something.
fact: A germ can infect a wound if the wound is not kept clean.
fact: Signs of an infected cut include redness spreading, swelling, heat, pus and pain. An adult should then get medical help.
fact: Washing hands and covering coughs stop germs infecting other people.
fact: Infected can also mean a computer has a harmful program in it, which can lose data.
exercise: «Ask an adult to take out a splinter with clean tweezers, because a splinter left in can get infected.» What does infected mean here? | Pulled out cleanly | *Having harmful germs growing in it | Happy and calm | Made of wood
exercise: «Cat scratches and bites can get infected, so they should be washed with soap and water.» Why should they be washed? | To make them smell nice | *To stop germs growing in them | To make the cat happy | To make them bigger
exercise: Sam says an infected computer is one that is clean and fast. What does infected mean for a computer? | It has been washed with soap | *It has a harmful program in it, like a virus | It is very fast and clean | It has a harmful program in it
test: «She was infected with flu.» What does infected mean here? | *Caught an illness from germs | Happy and laughing | Cut open by a doctor | Covered in dirt, like a muddy field
test: Which sign shows that a cut may be infected? | A small scab that is flat | A cut that is clean and dry | A cut that has stopped bleeding quickly | *Redness spreading, swelling and pus
exam: What does infected mean in «The whole class was infected by her laughter»? | Lost all its files | Covered in germs | *Filled with a feeling that spreads | Caught flu from a friend
